course: dictionary
lesson: 6706
title: Odour and other smells
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An odour is a smell. We usually notice odours when they are unpleasant, like «a strange odour came from the bin». The word strange tells you it was a smell you did not expect. Odour is a noun, so it is a thing: an odour, some odours.
explain: Use the words around odour to work out its meaning. A strong odour is a powerful smell, and a faint odour is a weak one. Odourless means it has no smell at all. To check, swap in the word smell: «a strange smell came from the bin» still makes sense, so odour means smell.
explain: In health lessons, body odour (BO) is the bad smell of sweat on someone's body. «"Body odour" (BO) is the polite name for the smell of sweat.» Polite names make embarrassing things sound gentler, so body odour sounds nicer than sweaty smell.
explain: Odour and odor are the same word spelled two ways. Britain, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland write odour; the USA writes odor. The meaning is always the same.
fact: An odour is a smell, often an unpleasant one.
fact: «Body odour» (BO) is the smell of sweat on your body, and washing stops it.
fact: Odourless means having no smell at all.
fact: Some gases have no odour, so smell is not a safe test; gas companies add an odour to cooking gas so leaks can be noticed.
fact: The USA spells this word odor; the UK spells it odour.
exercise: «a strange odour came from the bin» What is an odour? | *A smell | A loud noise | A type of bin | A dark colour
exercise: Gas companies add an odour to cooking gas. Why? | To change the colour of the gas | *So leaks can be noticed | To make the gas heavier | To stop the gas being used
exercise: Find and copy the word that means having no smell at all. | strong | sweaty | *odourless | faint
test: What is body odour? | A kind of soap | A pet's food bowl | The bright colour of a flower | *The smell of sweat on someone's body
test: What is a faint odour? | A very loud noise | *A weak smell | A sticky sweet | A bright light
exam: Which is the American spelling of odour? | ordour | odore | odour | *odor
